//@version=5
// NON-VACUITY CONTROL FOR THE IMPORT GATE -- this script MUST be refused.
// It draws a label and nothing else: there is no contentful output for the
// product to carry, which is what the `pine:presentation-only` guard exists to
// catch. If the harness reports this importable, its Apply step is not reading a
// real refusal and every IMPORT result it prints is unearned.
//
// (Its predecessor here paired `label.new` WITH a `plot(close)` and was ACCEPTED
// and drawn -- correctly, since the plot is real content. That is a
// presentation-loss case, not a refusal case, and conflating the two is how a
// control ends up proving nothing.)
indicator("Control No Contentful Output", overlay = true)
if barstate.islast
    label.new(bar_index, high, "hi")
